      "value": "This is happening to me too, and has been happening for a while. Super annoying when facing generally away from mirror, but small turns of head bring mirror back into view and produce a lag spike. I'd prefer persistently low performance from having the mirror always rendering as opposed to lag spikes.\nMy specs are Ryzen 2700X, Vega64, 64GB RAM, updated Win10.\nNone of my friends observe this behaviour, but most of them are on Nvidia cards, so this could be an AMD-specific issue.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
