      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I'm guessing somewhat, but this is likely due to the allocation/reordering of VRAM when a mirror is toggled. The hitch is more likely to occur in maps with larger textures in VRAM, or when many avatars are present (and are also eating VRAM).\n\nIf that is the case (and again, guessing somewhat), there's not much to be done except to reduce VRAM usage in worlds where mirrors are present by lowering texture size.\n\n(FWIW, I get it too on my 2080, but the hitch is usually no more than a second or so)",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
