      "value": "@{5acad9ecc9dba010c9c3ec68|full_name}: It does seem that it is VRAM-related, but I don't see the situation improving on its own. It still happens on GPUs with 11GB of VRAM, and 16GB models aren't exactly out yet.\nI wouldn't mind the freeze when toggling the mirror via a button in the world, but getting freezes when turning my head is the main issue. Would be nice to be able to have the mirror constantly enabled (or at least whatever part of it that allocates VRAM) regardless of view direction to reduce lag spikes.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
