  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "So mirrors in VRChat occlude when out of my view, and when I turn my head and a mirror enters my view, the entire game hitches for a few seconds before returning to normal. When they exit, this does not happen. FPS when they're in view depends on world but in the Home it's at a stable 90. Checking SteamVR's performance graphs, OpenHardwareMonitor, and my GPU drivers all show my CPU and GPU usage both plummet during these hitches, which makes it seem like it's not an issue with my GPU or CPU being overloaded, and more an issue with VRChat. Would be grateful if anyone could either help or look into this! Ty! ^-^\n\nUseful specs:\n\nRyzen 5 1600 @ 3.6GHz\n\nRX 470 4GB @ 1370MHz\n\n8GB DDR4 RAM 2133MHz\n\nWindows 7 64-bit (means no async compute sadly)",
